course: dictionary
lesson: 7581
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one to use. The word «pretty» is a good example. In «a pretty dress», pretty means nice to look at, in a gentle way.
explain: In «It's pretty easy», pretty does not describe anything. It is an adverb that means fairly or quite. Test it by swapping in fairly: «It's fairly easy» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Pretty can also mean very nearly, as in «pretty much the same». Here the words around it, same and much, tell you it means almost. When one word has several meanings, read the whole sentence before you decide.
fact: Pretty can be an adjective or an adverb.
fact: As an adjective, «a pretty dress» means nice to look at, in a gentle way.
fact: As an adverb, «pretty good» means fairly good, or quite good.
fact: In informal talk, «pretty much the same» means very nearly the same.
fact: A good check is to swap in another word, such as fairly or nearly, and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The meadow was full of pretty flowers.» What does pretty mean here? | Quite a lot of | Very loud | *Nice to look at | Very nearly
exercise: «The film was pretty good, but a bit long.» What does pretty mean here? | Very nearly | Lost and confused | *Fairly, or quite | Nice to look at
exercise: Ella says, «I'm pretty sure the shop is open.» What does pretty mean here? | Not sure at all | Nice to look at | Very loud and certain | *Fairly sure
test: «The old town was pretty much the same as I remembered.» What does pretty much mean here? | *Very nearly | Only at night | Very beautiful | Quickly
test: «The blue boudoir was a small, pretty sitting-room.» What does pretty mean here? | Loud and noisy | Fairly or quite | *Nice to look at, in a gentle way | Very nearly
exam: «It's pretty easy, so you can finish quickly.» What does pretty mean here? | Very loud | Very nearly | *Fairly or quite | Nice to look at
